{
 "about": "The race tree on the Season page (6.96.0): event distances per line, each opened by the one before it. Generic, the same for every person; the page fills it from the person's own Garmin record and races.json. A single sport node is Done when one session covered its distance (a race, or training: 'Covered in training'); a triathlon node is Done only by a finished race, and its legs show which single sport nodes are already covered. The next node on a line is Open; the rest are Locked. A planned or registered race is pinned on the node of its distance. Gates are a proposal until the package owner confirms them (tree_meta confirmed, a date). km is the distance in kilometres; legs is sport:km joined by ','; after is the node it needs first. A registered, planned or finished race longer than a line's top node adds its own node on top (the page does it, nothing is written here); beyond in tree_meta is the hint shown on each line's dashed ring above the top (line:label joined by ',').",
